export const visualLibraryPrompt = "The following is the OpenUI 1.0 language specification for an optional visual block within a ScholarLite answer. It applies only inside an openui code fence.\n\n## Syntax Rules\n\n1. Each statement is on its own line: `identifier = Expression`\n2. `root` is the entry point — every program must define `root = Col(...)`\n3. Expressions are: strings (\"...\"), numbers, booleans (true/false), null, arrays ([...]), objects ({...}), or component calls TypeName(arg1, arg2, ...)\n4. Use references for readability: define `name = ...` on one line, then use `name` later\n5. EVERY variable (except root) MUST be referenced by at least one other variable. Unreferenced variables are silently dropped and will NOT render. Always include defined variables in their parent's children/items array.\n6. Arguments are POSITIONAL (order matters, not names). Write `SomeComp([children], \"row\", \"l\")` NOT `SomeComp([children], direction: \"row\", gap: \"l\")` — colon syntax is NOT supported and silently breaks\n7. Optional arguments can be omitted from the end\n8. Declare mutable state with `$varName = defaultValue`. Components marked with `$binding` can read/write these. Undeclared $variables are auto-created with null default.\n9. String concatenation: `\"text\" + $var + \"more\"`\n10. Dot member access: `query.field` reads a field; on arrays it extracts that field from every element\n11. Index access: `arr[0]`, `data[index]`\n12. Arithmetic operators: +, -, *, /, % (work on numbers; + is string concat when either side is a string)\n13. Comparison: ==, !=, >, <, >=, <=\n14. Logical: &&, ||, ! (prefix)\n15. Ternary: `condition ? valueIfTrue : valueIfFalse`\n16. Parentheses for grouping: `(a + b) * c`\n- Strings use double quotes with backslash escaping\n\n## Component Signatures\n\nArguments marked with ? are optional. Sub-components can be inline or referenced; prefer references for better streaming.\nProps typed `ActionExpression` accept one @step, or Action([@steps...]) for several. See the Action section for available steps (@ToAssistant, @OpenUrl, @Set, @Reset).\nProps marked `$binding<type>` accept a `$variable` reference for two-way binding.\n\n### Layout\nCol(children: Node[], gap?: number, align?: \"start\" | \"center\" | \"end\" | \"stretch\") — Vertical layout. Without gap it spaces blocks like an article.\nRow(children: Node[], gap?: number, align?: \"start\" | \"center\" | \"end\" | \"stretch\", justify?: \"start\" | \"center\" | \"end\" | \"between\", wrap?: boolean) — Horizontal layout; items are vertically centered.\nBox(children?: Node[], direction?: \"row\" | \"col\", gap?: number, padding?: number, background?: Color, radius?: Radius, border?: boolean, width?: Length, height?: Length, flex?: number, align?: \"start\" | \"center\" | \"end\" | \"stretch\", justify?: \"start\" | \"center\" | \"end\" | \"between\", wrap?: boolean) — Flex container, a column by default. radius also clips the content.\nGrid(children: Node[], columns?: number, minChildWidth?: number, gap?: number) — Equal columns (default 2). With minChildWidth (px), columns drop on narrow screens.\nCard(children: Node[], variant?: \"outline\" | \"soft\", padding?: number, gap?: number) — Panel with a border; soft is a filled panel for summaries.\nDivider()\nSpacer() — Fills the free space in a Row.\ngap and padding count 4px steps. Use Col for narrow reading sidebars; Grid should set minChildWidth. Avoid nesting cards.\nColor tokens: ink, muted, faint, surface, info, success, warning, danger, purple, pink, chart1 to chart6. Use tokens for dark mode.\n\n### Text and evidence\nTitle(text: string, size?: \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\" | \"xl\" | \"2xl\" | \"3xl\", color?: Color) — Heading; md for a card title, lg for a section, 2xl for a big number.\nText(text: string | Node[], size?: \"xs\" | \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\", color?: Color, weight?: \"normal\" | \"medium\" | \"semibold\", italic?: boolean, lineThrough?: boolean, tabularNums?: boolean, maxLines?: number) — Paragraph; supports **bold**, *italic*, `code` and [links](https://…). text may be a list mixing strings and inline components: [Icon(\"clock\", \"sm\"), \" 25 min · \", Badge(\"Easy\")].\nCaption(text: string, color?: Color) — Small secondary text.\nLabel(text: string) — Field or group label.\nBadge(text: string, color?: \"neutral\" | \"info\" | \"success\" | \"warning\" | \"danger\" | \"purple\" | \"pink\") — Short status tag.\nList(items: (string | ListItem)[], marker?: \"bullet\" | \"number\" | \"none\", timeline?: boolean) — timeline joins the markers with a line.\nListItem(title: string, description?: string, marker?: string, children?: Node[]) — marker replaces the bullet or number, e.g. a time or an emoji.\nMarkdown(text: string) — Prose with headings, lists, quotes, code and tables.\nTable(columns: string[], rows: any[][]) — Each row lists its cells in column order; a cell may be a component. Number columns align right.\n\n### Charts\nChart(type: \"bar\" | \"line\" | \"area\" | \"pie\" | \"donut\" | \"scatter\", data: Record<string, string | number>[], x?: string, series?: string[], format?: \"number\" | \"currency\" | \"percent\", currency?: string, stacked?: boolean, height?: number) — Use at most 100 rows and 6 series. Every plotted value must be a finite number; never encode missing values as zero. Pie/donut require exactly one nonnegative series with positive total. Stacked charts require nonnegative values. x is the category key (a number key for scatter), series the value keys (default: every number key). percent values are like 45; currency is a code like \"EUR\".\nPreserve original units and comparable conditions. Missing data is not zero. Put data provenance and units in adjacent Title/Caption.\n\n### Local interactive exploration\nButton(label: string, action?: ActionExpression, variant?: \"solid\" | \"outline\" | \"soft\" | \"ghost\", disabled?: boolean) — Run an explicit local @Set/@Reset action, or request a follow-up with @ToAssistant. Follow-up text goes to the composer for review.\nSelect(value: $binding<string>, options: (string | {value: string, label: string})[], label?: string, placeholder?: string) — Dropdown, for long option lists.\nSegmentedControl(value: $binding<string>, options: (string | {value: string, label: string})[], block?: boolean) — 2 to 4 short choices in a row.\nSlider(value: $binding<number>, min: number, max: number, step?: number, label?: string, unit?: string, marks?: {value: number, label: string}[]) — Shows label and value; unit like \"%\" or \"$\" formats the value.\nControls bind to $variables. Display the result of each control. Calculations update locally without model calls.\n@ToAssistant only adds a follow-up draft for user review. Do not use @OpenUrl, @Run, Query or Mutation.\n\n### Mechanism drawings\nSvg(children: Node[], viewBox: string, width?: Length, height?: Length) — A drawing for steps, parts, mechanisms, diagrams and layouts. Scales to its width; its shapes take expressions, so state can move them.\nCircle(cx: number, cy: number, r: number, fill?: Color, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number)\nEllipse(cx: number, cy: number, rx: number, ry: number, fill?: Color, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number)\nRect(x: number, y: number, width: number, height: number, fill?: Color, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number, rx?: number)\nLine(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number)\nPath(d: string, fill?: Color, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number)\nPolyline(points: string, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, fill?: Color, opacity?: number) — points like \"0,0 10,5 20,0\".\nPolygon(points: string, fill?: Color, stroke?: Color, strokeWidth?: number, opacity?: number)\nG(children: Node[], transform?: string, opacity?: number) — Group; transform like \"rotate(30 50 50)\" or \"translate(10 0)\".\nSvgText(text: string, x: number, y: number, size?: number, fill?: Color, anchor?: \"start\" | \"middle\" | \"end\", weight?: \"normal\" | \"medium\" | \"semibold\")\nUse a compact viewBox (about 320 wide), readable labels and arrows. Never encode external assets or executable content.\n\n## Built-in Functions\n\nData functions prefixed with `@` to distinguish from components. These are the ONLY functions available — do NOT invent new ones.\nUse @-prefixed built-in functions (@Count, @Sum, @Avg, @Min, @Max, @Round) on data. Do NOT hardcode computed values.\n\n@Count(array: any[]) → number — Returns array length\n@First(array: any[]) → any — Returns first element of array\n@Last(array: any[]) → any — Returns last element of array\n@Sum(numbers: number[]) → number — Sum of numeric array\n@Avg(numbers: number[]) → number — Average of numeric array\n@Min(numbers: number[]) → number — Minimum value in array\n@Max(numbers: number[]) → number — Maximum value in array\n@Sort(array: any[], field: string, direction?: \"asc\" | \"desc\") → any[] — Sort array by field. Direction: \"asc\" (default) or \"desc\"\n@Filter(array: any[], field: string, operator: \"==\" | \"!=\" | \">\" | \"<\" | \">=\" | \"<=\" | \"contains\", value: any) → any[] — Filter array by field value\n@Round(number: number, decimals?: number) → number — Round to N decimal places (default 0)\n@Abs(number: number) → number — Absolute value\n@Floor(number: number) → number — Round down to nearest integer\n@Ceil(number: number) → number — Round up to nearest integer\n@Each(array: any[], varName: string, template: any) — Evaluate template for each element. varName is the loop variable — use it ONLY inside the template expression (inline). Do NOT create a separate statement for the template.\n@Pow(base: number, exponent: number) → number — base raised to exponent\n@Sqrt(number: number) → number — Square root; null for negative input\n@Clamp(value: number, min: number, max: number) → number — Bound a value between min and max\n@Percent(part: number, total: number) → number — part / total × 100; null if total is zero\n@Format(value: number, kind?: \"number\" | \"percent\" | \"compact\", decimals?: number) → string — Format a finite number with up to decimals digits; percent takes 45 for 45%\n\nBuiltins compose — output of one is input to the next:\n`@Count(@Filter(data.rows, \"field\", \"==\", \"val\"))` for KPIs/chart values, `@Round(@Avg(data.rows.score), 1)`, `@Each(data.rows, \"item\", Comp(item.field))` for per-item rendering.\nArray pluck: `data.rows.field` extracts a field from every row → use with @Sum, @Avg, charts, tables.\n\nIMPORTANT @Each rule: The loop variable (e.g. \"item\") is ONLY available inside the @Each template expression. Always inline the template — do NOT extract it to a separate statement.\nCORRECT: `list = @Each(rows, \"t\", Comp(t.name))`\nWRONG: `item = Comp(t.name)` then `list = @Each(rows, \"t\", item)`, because t is undefined in item.\n\n## Action — Button Behavior\n\nAn action wires a button click to operations. Pass one @-prefixed step bare, e.g. Button(\"Ask\", @ToAssistant(\"Tell me more\")). Put several steps in Action([...]), e.g. Button(\"Read\", Action([@OpenUrl(\"https://example.com\"), @ToAssistant(\"Summarize this page\")])). Steps execute in order.\nButtons without an action automatically send their label to the assistant (equivalent to @ToAssistant(label)).\n\nAvailable steps:\n- @ToAssistant(message: string, context?: any) — Send a message to the assistant (for conversational buttons like \"Tell me more\", \"Explain this\"). The optional context is any value (object, array, string, number) passed to the assistant as hidden data, e.g. @ToAssistant(\"Show details\", {orderId: 42})\n- @OpenUrl(url: string) — Navigate to a URL\n- @Set(variable: $variable, value: any) — Set a $variable to a specific value\n- @Reset(variable: $variable) — Reset $variables to their declared defaults; pass several to reset each (e.g. @Reset($title, $priority) restores $title=\"\" and $priority=\"medium\")\n\nExample — simple nav:\n```\nviewBtn = Button(\"View\", @OpenUrl(\"https://example.com\"))\n```\n\n- An action can be assigned to a variable or inlined: Button(\"Go\", onSubmit) and Button(\"Go\", Action([...])) both work\n\n## Hoisting & Streaming (CRITICAL)\n\nopenui-lang supports hoisting: a reference can be used BEFORE it is defined. The parser resolves all references after the full input is parsed.\n\nDuring streaming, the output is re-parsed on every chunk. Undefined references are temporarily unresolved and appear once their definitions stream in. This creates a progressive top-down reveal — structure first, then data fills in.\n\n**Recommended statement order for optimal streaming:**\n1. `root = Col(...)` — UI shell appears immediately\n2. $variable declarations — state ready for bindings\n3. Component definitions — fill in with data already available\n4. Data values — leaf content last\n\nAlways write the root = Col(...) statement first so the UI shell appears immediately, even before child data has streamed in.\n## Important Rules\n- Choose components that best represent the content (tables for comparisons, charts for trends, forms for input, etc.)\n\n## Final Verification\nBefore finishing, walk your output and verify:\n1. root = Col(...) is the FIRST line (for optimal streaming).\n2. Every referenced name is defined. Every defined name (other than root) is reachable from root.\n3. Every $binding appears in at least one component or expression.\n\n- Object keys containing non-ASCII characters must always be double-quoted, for example {\"方案\": \"A\", \"延迟\": 12}. ASCII keys are recommended.\n- Only use this registered library. Keep diagrams and charts readable in a 300px-wide column.\n- Numbers must come from supplied material or be explicitly labeled as hypothetical; do not invent measurements.\n- Use an interactive control only when changing it meaningfully changes the displayed result.\n- No network, external URL actions, Query, Mutation, or executable HTML is available.";
